//
// A CONSTANT A NULLABLE NARROW TUPLE MEMBER CANNOT HOLD IS REFUSED (`@FR-N-Reserve` crossed with
// `@FR-L-Tuple`).  N-Reserve: "A CONSTANT outside a nullable narrow slot's usable range (`255` …
// into a `u8?`) is REFUSED at compile time, since it could only be stored as null", and a tuple
// member is such a slot (L-Tuple lays it out as a field).  The N-Reserve cell `1796-…` measures
// a vector element; this one moves the slot to a member of a tuple literal bound to a declared
// tuple local.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: 255 does not fit `u8?`
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the constant and the type.
// HOLDS: `a-nullable-narrow-tuple-member-spends-its-top-code-in-every-place` beside it.

fn main() {
  t: (u8?, integer) = (255, 1);
  assert(t.1 == 1, "unreachable");
}
